course: dictionary
lesson: 12196
title: Confined: kept within limits
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Confined» means kept inside a small or closed space, or kept from going somewhere. It is the past form of the verb confine, which means to keep something within limits.
explain: «The sick cat was confined to the house until it got better.» The cat could not go out. Confined to the house means kept inside the house, and the clue is that the cat was ill and needed rest.
explain: Look at the words around confined. «Confined spaces» like tanks and tunnels are dangerous because there is not much fresh air. In «The problem is confined to one class», confined to means only in one class.
fact: Confined means kept inside a small or closed space, or kept from going somewhere.
fact: «Confined to bed» means kept in bed, usually because you are ill.
fact: «Confined space» means a small, closed place, such as a tank or a tunnel.
fact: «Confined to» can also mean only in: «The problem is confined to one class» means it is found in that class only.
fact: Confine is the verb, and confined is its past form: «The farmer confined the hens to the barn.»
exercise: «The sick boy was confined to bed for a week.» What does confined to bed mean? | *Kept in bed, because he was ill | Brave and happy | Sent to school | Sleeping very deeply
exercise: «Never go into a confined space without a safety check.» What is a confined space? | A fast train | *A small, closed place, like a tank | A room with a window | Any big open field
exercise: «The farmer confined the hens to the barn.» Find and copy the word that tells you the hens were kept inside. | farmer | hens | *confined | barn
test: «The mistake was confined to one page of the book.» What does confined mean here? | *Limited to one page | Locked in a box | Very long | Kept from going anywhere
test: Why would a doctor say a patient must stay confined to bed? | *Because the patient is ill and needs rest | Because beds are fun | Because the patient is very fast | Because the patient wants to go to school
exam: What does «The problem is confined to one class» mean? | The class is very small and cramped | *The problem is limited to that one class only | The problem was solved in class | The problem is in every class in the school
